# LLM Instructions: CRIT — Curated Recommendations In Titles

This document contains everything an LLM coding assistant (e.g. Claude Code) needs to
recreate this project from scratch. Follow each section in order.

---

## Project Overview

A web-based game recommendation system that:
- Connects to Steam (via API key), Epic Games (OAuth), and GOG (OAuth)
- Enriches game libraries with ratings from RAWG (a free game database)
- Uses Claude AI to recommend games from three modes: "From Library", "Steam Deals", "Backlog"
- Streams Claude's response in real-time via Server-Sent Events (SSE)
- Also ships a CLI mode for terminal use

Stack: Python 3.11+, FastAPI, uvicorn, anthropic SDK, vanilla JS frontend (no build step).

