## 4. Steam Connector — `game_recommender/steam.py`

Single public function: `get_steam_library(api_key=None, user_id=None) -> list[Game]`

Behavior:
- Falls back to env vars `STEAM_API_KEY`, `STEAM_USER_ID` if args are None
- Raises `ValueError` if either is missing (with helpful message including setup URL)
- Calls `https://api.steampowered.com/IPlayerService/GetOwnedGames/v0001/` with params:
  `key`, `steamid`, `include_appinfo=True`, `include_played_free_games=True`, `format=json`
- Timeout: 10 seconds
- If `data["response"]` exists but is empty `{}`, raises `RuntimeError` (private profile message)
- Maps each game: `name = g.get("name", f"App {g['appid']}")`, `app_id = str(g["appid"])`,
  `playtime_minutes = g.get("playtime_forever", 0)`,
  `last_played = str(g["rtime_last_played"]) if g.get("rtime_last_played") else None`
- Returns games sorted by `playtime_minutes` descending

