## 5. Epic Games Connector — `game_recommender/epic.py`

Uses the unofficial Epic launcher OAuth2 flow (reverse-engineered from Legendary/EpicResearch).

Constants:
```python
_CLIENT_ID     = "34a02cf8f4414e29b15921876da36f9a"
_CLIENT_SECRET = "daafbccc737745039dffe53d94fc76cf"
EPIC_AUTH_URL  = f"https://www.epicgames.com/id/api/redirect?clientId={_CLIENT_ID}&responseType=code"
_TOKEN_URL     = "https://account-public-service-prod03.ol.epicgames.com/account/api/oauth/token"
_LIBRARY_URL   = "https://library-service.live.use1a.on.epicgames.com/library/api/public/items"
```

Helper `_basic_auth() -> str`: returns `"Basic " + base64(f"{_CLIENT_ID}:{_CLIENT_SECRET}")`

**`exchange_code(auth_code: str) -> dict`**
- POST to `_TOKEN_URL` with header `Authorization: Basic ...` and `Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded`
- Body: `grant_type=authorization_code&code=<auth_code>`
- Timeout: 15s. Returns JSON. Raises `requests.HTTPError` on failure.

**`refresh_tokens(refresh_token: str) -> dict`**
- Same as above but body: `grant_type=refresh_token&refresh_token=<token>`

**`get_epic_library(access_token: str) -> list[Game]`**
- Uses a `requests.Session` with header `Authorization: Bearer <token>`
- Cursor-based pagination: GET `_LIBRARY_URL?includeMetadata=true[&cursor=<cursor>]`
  - Extend a `records` list from `data["records"]`
  - Next cursor from `data["responseMetadata"]["nextCursor"]` — stop when empty/None
- For each record:
  - `title = (metadata.get("title") or r.get("appName") or r.get("catalogId", "")).strip()`
  - Skip if blank, already seen, or (len==32 and fully alphanumeric — internal ID heuristic)
  - `app_id = r.get("catalogId") or r.get("appName")`
  - Platform is "epic"; `playtime_minutes` is always 0 (Epic exposes no playtime)
- Returns games sorted alphabetically by `name.lower()`

Auth flow note for users:
1. Direct to `EPIC_AUTH_URL` while logged into epicgames.com
2. Page returns JSON — user copies the `authorizationCode` value
3. Call `exchange_code(auth_code)` → get tokens → call `get_epic_library(access_token)`

