## 6. GOG Connector — `game_recommender/gog.py`

Uses the unofficial GOG Galaxy OAuth2 flow.

Constants:
```python
_CLIENT_ID     = "46899977096215655"
_CLIENT_SECRET = "9d85c43b1482497dbbce61f6e4aa173a433796eeae2ca8c5f6129f2dc4de46d9"
_REDIRECT_URI  = "https://embed.gog.com/on_login_success?origin=client"
_TOKEN_URL     = "https://auth.gog.com/token"
_PRODUCTS_URL  = "https://embed.gog.com/account/getFilteredProducts"
GOG_AUTH_URL   = (
    f"https://auth.gog.com/auth?client_id={_CLIENT_ID}"
    f"&redirect_uri={_REDIRECT_URI}&response_type=code&layout=client2"
)
```

**`exchange_code(auth_code: str) -> dict`**
- GET (not POST) to `_TOKEN_URL` with query params:
  `client_id`, `client_secret`, `grant_type=authorization_code`, `code`, `redirect_uri`
- Timeout 15s. Raises `requests.HTTPError` on failure.

**`refresh_tokens(refresh_token: str) -> dict`**
- GET to `_TOKEN_URL` with `grant_type=refresh_token&refresh_token=<token>` (plus client creds)

**`get_gog_library(access_token: str) -> list[Game]`**
- Header: `Authorization: Bearer <token>`
- Page-based pagination: GET `_PRODUCTS_URL?mediaType=1&page=<N>`
- For each product: `title = (product.get("title") or "").strip()`, skip if blank
- `app_id = str(product.get("id", ""))`
- Stop when `page >= data.get("totalPages", 1)`
- Platform "gog", `playtime_minutes` always 0
- Returns sorted alphabetically by `name.lower()`

Auth flow note: GOG only allows `embed.gog.com` as redirect URI, so the app cannot receive
the callback directly. Users must copy the `code` parameter from the popup URL bar.

