## 7. RAWG Ratings — `game_recommender/ratings.py`

Module-level cache: `_SEARCH_CACHE: dict[str, Optional[GameRating]] = {}`

**`get_game_rating(game_name, api_key=None, *, delay=0.25) -> Optional[GameRating]`**
- Cache key: `game_name.lower()`; return cached value if present (including cached None)
- Fall back to `RAWG_API_KEY` env var; raise `ValueError` if missing
- `time.sleep(delay)` before every request (polite rate limiting)
- GET `https://api.rawg.io/api/games?key=<key>&search=<name>&page_size=1`, timeout 10s
- If no results, cache and return None
- Map first result: `rawg_rating`, `rawg_ratings_count`, `metacritic_score`, `genres` (list of names),
  `tags` (list of names, **capped at 10**), `released`, `background_image`
- `name = r.get("name", game_name)` (fallback to query name)
- Store in cache, return `GameRating`

**`enrich_games(games, api_key=None, progress_callback=None) -> list[GameWithRating]`**
- For each game, optionally call `progress_callback(i+1, total, game.name)`, then call
  `get_game_rating(game.name, api_key=api_key)`
- Returns `list[GameWithRating]`

