## 9. Claude Recommender — `game_recommender/recommender.py`

**`get_recommendations(games, user_preferences=None, num_recommendations=5, api_key=None, stream_output=True) -> str`**
- Falls back to `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY` env var; raises `ValueError` if missing
- Creates `anthropic.Anthropic(api_key=api_key)`
- Builds library text via `_format_library_for_prompt(games)`:
  - Each line: `- {name} ({PLATFORM}) | {X}h played` (or "unplayed")
  - Append RAWG, Metacritic, genres (first 3) if rating exists
- Computes `played` (playtime > 0) and `unplayed` counts for library stats
- Prompt instructs Claude to recommend exactly N games, each with: "Why play this now",
  "Ratings", "Best for" (session type), "Similar to" (other library games). End with
  a brief overall note about library patterns.
- Model: `"claude-opus-4-6"`, `max_tokens=4096`, `thinking={"type": "adaptive"}`
- If `stream_output=True`: use `client.messages.stream()`, print each text chunk, return joined string
- If False: use `client.messages.create()`, extract the first text block

