## 11. CLI Entry Point — `main.py`

Uses `click` for CLI, `rich` for output, `python-dotenv` for env loading.

Calls `load_dotenv()` at module level.

CLI options:
- `--epic-library FILE` — path to Epic library JSON
- `--gog-library FILE` — path to GOG library JSON
- `--other-library FILE` — path to custom library JSON
- `--no-steam` (flag) — skip Steam
- `--no-ratings` (flag) — skip RAWG enrichment
- `--top N` (default 50) — only send top N games to LLM
- `--count N` (default 5) — number of recommendations
- `--preferences TEXT` — user mood/preference text
- `--init-epic` (flag) — write sample epic.json and exit
- `--init-gog` (flag) — write sample gog.json and exit
- `--list-library` (flag) — print library table and exit

Workflow in `main()`:
1. Handle `--init-epic` / `--init-gog` first (call `create_example_json`, return)
2. Try Steam if not `--no-steam` and both env vars are set (warn if missing, don't crash)
3. Load Epic/GOG/other from JSON files if paths provided
4. Exit with error if no games loaded
5. Sort all games by `playtime_minutes` descending
6. If `--list-library`: print Rich table and return
7. Enrich top N games with RAWG (if key available and not `--no-ratings`)
8. Call `get_recommendations(..., stream_output=True)`

`_print_library_table(games, max_rows=50)`: Rich table with columns #, Game, Platform, Playtime.
Shows "...and N more" footer if truncated.

