### Security headers middleware

Add middleware that sets these headers on every response:
- `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`
- `X-Frame-Options: DENY`
- `Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin`
- `Content-Security-Policy`: allow scripts from `self` and `cdn.jsdelivr.net`; images from `self data:`; connect-src `self`

### Session store

```python
_sessions: dict[str, dict] = {}
```

`_get_session(session_id) -> (str, dict)`: if valid ID exists, return it; else create new UUID, store empty dict, return both.

`_set_session_cookie(response, session_id)`: set cookie `session_id`, httponly=True, samesite="strict", secure=`_COOKIE_SECURE`, max_age=8 hours.

### Routes

**`GET /`** → reads and returns `web/templates/index.html` as `HTMLResponse`

**`GET /auth/epic/start`**
- Gets/creates session, builds callback URL from `request.base_url`
- Redirects to:
  `https://www.epicgames.com/id/authorize?client_id=34a02cf8f4414e29b15921876da36f9a&response_type=code&redirect_uri=<callback>&scope=basic_profile`
- Sets session cookie on the redirect response

**`GET /auth/epic/callback`** (receives `?code=` or `?error=`)
- On error/missing code: redirect to `/?auth_error=<url_encoded_reason>`
- Calls `exchange_code(code)` via `asyncio.to_thread`; on failure redirect to `/?auth_error=...`
- Stores `epic: {access_token, refresh_token, account_id}` in session
- Redirects to `/?auth_success=epic`

**`GET /api/status`** → `{"steam": bool, "epic": bool, "gog": bool}`

**`POST /api/auth/steam`**
- Body: `{"api_key": "...", "user_id": "..."}`; strip both; 400 if blank
- Validate by calling Steam `GetOwnedGames` via `httpx.AsyncClient`
- 400 if non-200 or empty response object
- Store `steam: {api_key, user_id}` in session
- Return `{"ok": true, "game_count": N}` with session cookie

**`POST /api/auth/epic`**
- Body: `{"auth_code": "..."}`; 400 if blank
- `exchange_code(auth_code)` via `asyncio.to_thread`; 400 on any exception
- Store `epic: {access_token, refresh_token, account_id}` in session

**`POST /api/auth/gog`**
- Body: `{"auth_code": "..."}`; 400 if blank
- `exchange_code(auth_code)` via `asyncio.to_thread`; 400 on any exception
- Store `gog: {access_token, refresh_token, user_id}` in session

**`DELETE /api/auth/{platform}`**
- 404 if platform not in ("steam", "epic", "gog")
- Pop platform from session; return `{"ok": true}`

**`GET /api/library`** (query: `skip_ratings: bool = False`)
- 400 if no platforms connected
- Gather all platforms concurrently with `asyncio.gather(*tasks.values(), return_exceptions=True)`
- Each platform fetch is wrapped to attempt token refresh on failure (epic/gog)
- Sort merged list: `(-playtime_minutes, name.lower())`
- If not `skip_ratings` and `RAWG_API_KEY` set: enrich top 75 via `_enrich_with_rawg`
- Return `{"games": [...], "errors": [...]}`
- Each game dict: `name, platform, app_id, playtime_minutes, rawg_rating, metacritic, genres`

**`GET /api/recommend`** (SSE, query params: `mode, preferences, count, min_discount, include_wishlist, max_new_minutes`)
- 400 if no `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, no session, unknown mode, preferences > 500 chars
- Clamp `count` to `max(1, min(count, 10))`
- Returns `StreamingResponse` with `media_type="text/event-stream"` and headers
  `Cache-Control: no-cache`, `X-Accel-Buffering: no`
- SSE event format: each event is `data: <json>\n\n`
  - `{"type": "status", "msg": "..."}` — progress updates
  - `{"text": "..."}` — Claude response chunks
  - `{"done": true}` — stream complete
  - `{"error": "..."}` — error; stream ends

SSE generator logic:
1. Yield status "Loading your library…"; call `get_library(skip_ratings=True)`; error if empty
2. **Mode "sales"**: fetch `_fetch_sales(min_discount, steam_creds, include_wishlist, owned_ids)`;
   error if no deals; build prompt with `_build_sales_prompt`
3. **Mode "new"**: filter `games_raw` where `playtime_minutes <= max_new_minutes`;
   error if none; build prompt with `_build_new_game_prompt`
4. **Mode "library"**: build prompt with `_build_library_prompt`
5. Yield status "Asking Claude…"
6. Use `anthropic.AsyncAnthropic` with `client.messages.stream()`;
   yield each text chunk as `{"text": chunk}`;
   yield `{"done": true}` on completion; `{"error": str(e)}` on exception

### Prompt builders

**`_build_library_prompt(games, preferences, count)`**: delegates to `_build_prompt`

**`_build_prompt(games, preferences, count)`**:
- Format up to 100 games, each line: `- {name} ({PLATFORM}) | {X}h played` (or "unplayed"),
  appending RAWG, Metacritic, genres if present
- Include library stats (total/played/unplayed) and preferences section
- Prompt asks for N recommendations, each with: "Why now", "Ratings", "Best for", "Similar to"
- End with 2-3 sentence insight about gaming taste patterns

**`_build_sales_prompt(games, sale_games, preferences, count)`**:
- Library lines (up to 80): `- {name} ({PLATFORM}) | {X}h played | genres`
- Sale lines (up to 50): tag (`⭐ WISHLIST` or `🛒 FEATURED`), name, discount%, sale price, original price, genres
- Ask Claude to recommend N deals, each with: "Why it fits", "Genre match", "Deal quality"
- End with verdict on whether this is a good sale

**`_build_new_game_prompt(games, unplayed, preferences, count)`**:
- Played lines (>60min, up to 60): `- {name} | {X}h | genres`
- Unplayed lines (up to 80): `- {name} ({PLATFORM}) | {mins}min | RAWG score | genres`
- Ask Claude to recommend N unplayed games, each with: "Why start now", "What to expect", "Best entry point"
- End with sentence about the hidden gem in the list

